 "brief": "The body of a small C-clamp in PETG (FDM, printed flat on its side, layers along Y), 16 mm thick (y = -8 to 8), inside x = 0 to 70, z = 0 to 90. The work goes in a throat open toward +X: nothing may be in x = 25 to 70 between z = 18 and z = 68. An M8 clamping screw runs down along Z at x = 50 through the upper jaw, in a threaded insert (10 mm outside) the full 22 mm depth of the jaw; it presses the work against an anvil pad on the lower jaw (x = 40 to 60, top at z = 18, 3 mm thick). Clamping force 400 N. Safety factor 2.",
